4. CONSUMER SWEEP — PASS. This is the check that killed wt-glm.
   a) buildCumulativeChartData (handlers.go:1044-1058): the one consumer
      that is NOT a FilterByType call. Its loop reads
        if t.TransactionType == models.Income { dayTotal += Abs(Amount) }
        else { dayTotal -= Abs(Amount) }
      so a Transfer row (not Income) falls in the else and is subtracted;
      a paired transfer subtracts twice. The merged code inserts, immediately
      before that if/else (handlers.go:1051-1053):
        if t.TransactionType == models.Transfer { continue }
      with a comment naming exactly this reasoning. Regression test
      TestBuildCumulativeChartData_SkipsTransfers (handlers_test.go:333)
      feeds a paired $2000 pair + a $3000 external leg + a $500 grocery +
      $5000 income and asserts cumulative[1]==5000 (transfer day moves
      nothing) and cumulative[2]==4500 (only grocery). Mutation check:
      remove the skip and the external(-3000)+food(-500) day yields
      5000-3500=1500 != 4500, and the transfer day yields 5000-4000=1000
      != 5000 — both assertions fail. Discriminating.
   b) I then enumerated every other consumer myself, not trusting the
      adjudication's list:
      - metrics.Calculate (metrics.go:100-105): income/outflows via
        FilterByType(models.Income/Outflow). Transfer excluded by type.
        TestCalculateMetrics_ExcludesTransfers (metrics_test.go:359) +
        TestLoadData_MetricsExcludeEveryTransferRow (transfers_test.go:132)
        hold it; the latter's fixture is hostile (credit leg "TRANSFER IN
        FROM SCHWAB" hits IncomeKeywords) so a leak lands in TotalIncome,
        not cancelled.
      - dashboard totals (handlers.go:351/356, 511/516, 616/620): all
        inc.SumAmount()/Abs(exp.SumAmount()) on FilterByType slices. Safe.
      - dashboard drilldown total (handlers.go:267): txns come from
        bucketMajorExpenses output, built from FilterByType(Outflow). Safe.
      - bucketMajorExpenses/unmatchedTotal (794-795, 822): operate on
        outflows slice. Safe.
      - buildSpendingTrendChart/buildMerchantsChart (910, 983): on
        FilterByType(Outflow). Safe.
      - insights trends (insights/trends.go:35,119,120,185,273,274,303)
        and recurring (recurring.go:223): all FilterByType(Outflow/Income).
        Safe.
      - mcpsvc/spend summary/search/trends/insights: summary.go:80,113,135;
        search.go:148,150; all FilterByType. insights.go:145 uses
        `t.TransactionType == models.Outflow && t.Amount < 0` — a
        composite guard that excludes Transfer (Transfer != Outflow). Safe.
      - majorexpenses engine.go:282,323: `!= models.Outflow` guard skips
        Transfer. Safe.
      - anomalies.go:161, pricecreep.go:81: same `== Outflow && Amount<0`
        composite guard. Safe.
      - near_duplicates.go:58 and major_expense_names.go:49:
        `!= models.Outflow` / `== models.Income` guards skip Transfer.
        Near-dup indexes outflows only, so a transfer drops out of
        near-duplicate candidacy automatically — documented by
        TestLoadData_TransferIsNotANearDuplicateCandidate.
      - explorer handlers.go:173,175,185,189,312,314,324,328: all
        FilterByType. Safe.
   No site treats "not Income" as "expense" without a FilterByType. The
   buildCumulativeChartData site was the only one, and it is fixed.

5. AUTO-PAIR DISCIPLINE — PASS.
   - Pattern-less coincidence NOT auto-paired: Classify step 3
     (transfers.go:210-222) only adds to `suspected`, never pairs.
     TestClassify_PatternlessCoincidenceIsSuggestedNotPaired asserts
     Paired==0 and Suspected==1 with Reason=amount_match.
     TestLoadData_PatternlessCoincidenceIsSuggestedNotPaired asserts
     the same end-to-end.
   - Ambiguous tie to review: Classify step 2 (transfers.go:194-206) —
     len(best)>1 sets ambiguous[i] and all best[j], queues them with
     ReasonAmbiguous, does NOT pair. Crucially, ambiguous rows are also
     withdrawn as candidates (the extra gate `!ambiguous[j]` at line 188)
     so a tied row cannot become someone else's "unique" candidate — the
     contagious-ambiguity insight the report flagged.
     TestClassify_AmbiguousTieGoesToReview asserts Paired==0, Suspected==2.
   - Same-account never pairs: isCandidatePair (transfers.go:366-375)
     returns false when a.AccountID==b.AccountID; two empty AccountIDs
     count as same account. TestClassify_SameAccountEqualAmountDoesNotPair
     and TestLoadData_SameAccountEqualAmountDoesNotPair both assert
     Paired==0 and Suspected==0.
   - Same-sign never pairs: isCandidatePair requires ca==-cb.
     TestClassify_SameSideAmountsDoNotPair.

